  "\"Okay, and?\" I dragged my words out, letting him know I didn't care about any of the small details.",
  "\"Well, Tyler refused to help them. Then, Tyler kept talking mess on the Crescent pack. He angered their",
  "Alpha, irritated him off real bad.\" Sean shook his head as if he were trying to get rid of a bad memory.",
  "\"He didn't.\" I sighed, shaking my head. I know Tyler's inflated ego was going to bite him in the ego. His father was a half-assed Alpha and he was turning out to be the same.",
  "\"They came here, Lola. They declared war on us.\" Sean frowned, glancing at Dad.",
  "I couldn't help but feel confused. Sure, there were a lot of new faces but everything seemed the same.",
  "There was no way Tyler defeated the Alpha of the Crescent pack.",
  "\"What happened?\" I frowned, looking between Sean and my Dad's grim faces.",
  "\"I'll tell you what happened,\" My dad spat angrily. \"Not a single seriously pack would help Tyler. Tyler made us all train. Everyone had to defend the pack. Your mom was lost during the conflict. I couldn't get to her in time.\" My dad's voice broke off with a mournful sigh.",
  "\"How- How could he do that.\" I said the words more to myself. I knew Tyler was bad, but this was worse than I could imagine. Then again, they hadn't finished the story.",
  "\"And you know what the worst part of all of this is? Tyler seriously ran. Grabbed his Brittany and escaped while the rest of us were fighting for our lives.\" My Dad spat, now he was shaking with anger.",
