  "\"Don't worry, Lola. If you're no good he won't make you train. He just likes to see what everyone is capable of.\" Sean told me, his frown permanently etched onto his face.",
  "\"I can fight just fine.\" I snapped at him. I no longer wanted to be treated like some dainty little girl. I may be small, but I can handle my own.",
